     "at": [
      1110,
      170
     ],
     "title": "Precharge and sample",
     "text": "No resistor on the wire. The pad makes the high level, one sample at a time."
    },
    {
     "from": 13.48,
     "to": 23.11,
     "anchor": [
      "c",
      "drv"
     ],
     "at": [
      1110,
      170
     ],
     "n": 1,
     "title": "Drive high, 100.0 ns",
     "text": "15 cycles of the 150 MHz system clock, at the pad's 2 mA drive strength."
    },
    {
     "from": 23.71,
     "to": 34.53,
     "anchor": [
      "c",
      "rpd"
     ],
     "at": [
      1110,
      170
     ],
     "n": 2,
     "style": "warn",
     "title": "Let go",
     "text": "3 kΩ × 72 pF = <b>216 ns</b>. The wire's own capacitance holds the level."
    },
    {
     "from": 35.129999999999995,
     "to": 42.400000000000006,
     "anchor": [
      "c",
      "in"
     ],
     "at": [
      1110,
      170
     ],
     "n": 3,
     "style": "ok",
     "title": "Sample, 113.3 ns later",
     "text": "17 cycles after the release. <b>1.93 V</b> on the wire: the bit is high."
    },
    {
     "from": 43.0,
     "to": 56.480000000000004,
     "anchor": [
      "c",
      "srv"
     ],
     "at": [
      1110,
      170
     ],
     "style": "warn",
     "title": "The servo pulls low",
     "text": "1.4 V while both drive, for 100 ns of every 1086.7 ns. At the sample the wire is at <b>0 V</b>."
    },
    {
     "from": 57.08,
     "to": 67.53,
     "anchor": [
      "c",
      "pad"
     ],
     "at": [
      1110,
      170
     ],
     "title": "7 PIO instructions",
     "text": "<b>set pindirs, 1</b> · <b>set pindirs, 0</b> · <b>in pins, 1</b> and 4 nop. 163 cycles a sample, 32 samples to a word."
    }
   ],
   "say": [
    {
     "at": 0.8,
     "text": "There is another way to make the high level. The pin makes it itself, for an instant, only while it listens, and then looks at what the servo does with it."
    },
    {
     "at": 13.18,
     "text": "The pad drives the wire high for 100 nanoseconds. That charges the capacitance of the wire and the servo's input to 3.3 volts."
    },
    {
     "at": 23.41,
     "text": "Then the pad lets go. The charge drains through the servo's 3 kilohm pull-down, and the voltage falls with a time constant of 216 nanoseconds."
    },
    {
     "at": 34.83,
     "text": "113 nanoseconds after the release, the pad samples the wire. It still holds 1.9 volts: a high."
    },
    {
     "at": 42.7,
     "text": "When the servo pulls low, the picture changes. The pad lifts the wire only part of the way, and 10 nanoseconds after the release the wire is back at ground. The sample reads low."
    },
    {
     "at": 56.78,
     "text": "One precharge, one sample, every 1087 nanoseconds. A second state machine of the RP2350's programmable I O does it in 7 instructions."
    }
   ]
  },
